  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 345 AM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nActive weather continues into Monday with the potential for \nwidespread rainfall continuing across the area. While the majority \nof the QPF will have fallen on Sunday and Sunday night, some areas, \nmainly across extreme north central Nebraska, could see an \nadditional half inch to 1 inch of new rainfall just on Monday alone. \nThe latest probabilities support this as the probability of seeing \nover a half inch is 90 percent or higher across areas east of US-83, \nand the probability of seeing over 1 inch is still over 80 percent \nfor these same areas. Therefore, confidence remains high that \nportions of the forecast area will see up to another inch on Monday \nbefore precipitation begins to push out of the area Monday night, \ncompletely exiting the area by Tuesday morning. Some additional low \nend (less than 25 percent) PoPs are then possible on Tuesday \nafternoon and evening as a weak trough pushes through the region. At \nthis point, not expecting much in the way of rainfall totals as any \nshower development will remain isolated in nature. Some embedded \nthunderstorms may also be possible with this Tuesday activity, but \nwith the best instability and forcing across eastern Nebraska, not \nanticipating any severe storms. Drier conditions return mid-week as \nweak upper level ridging and surface high pressure builds into the \nregion. Scattered showers return by late week, but confidence \nremains too low in development, timing, and strength to put much \nmore than a mention in the forecast at this time. \n\nFor temperatures, continued rain and clouds as well as cold air \nadvection into the region will keep temperatures cooler than normal \non Monday. Highs will only rise into the upper 40s to upper 50s, \nwith some locations across the Pine Ridge remaining in the low 40s. \nWarmer weather arrives Tuesday lasting through the end of the week \nas ridging builds back over Nebraska. A return to warm air advection \nand sunshine will allow temperatures to steadily rise back into the \nlow to mid 60s Tuesday through Friday.",
